From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sechost, advapi32: NotifyBootConfigStatus asks the service control manager (for fast-a, goes after 3214) (5903)

NotifyBootConfigStatus returned TRUE without asking anyone. It now calls the
svcctl RPC (RNotifyBootConfigStatus), exported from sechost and imported by
advapi32 as Windows does. The server side is fast-a 3214 (svcctl_NotifyBootConfigStatus:
ERROR_BOOT_ALREADY_ACCEPTED on the second acceptance, ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED for a refusal);
without it the server answers ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, so this patch must not go in alone.

Written by fast-b (work/for-fast-a, for after fast-a 3214); numbered 5903 at
integration (integ-2026-10).
---
--- a/dlls/sechost/service.c	2026-10-14 23:18:46.243362789 -0700
+++ b/dlls/sechost/service.c	2026-10-14 23:18:53.439340006 -0700
@@ -289,6 +289,32 @@
 }
 
 /******************************************************************************
+ *     NotifyBootConfigStatus   (sechost.@)
+ *
+ * Tells the service control manager that the boot configuration is (or is not) good.
+ * The server answers ERROR_BOOT_ALREADY_ACCEPTED to a second acceptance and
+ * ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED to a refusal (there is no last-known-good control set).
+ */
+BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH NotifyBootConfigStatus( BOOL boot_acceptable )
+{
+    DWORD err;
+
+    TRACE( "%d\n", boot_acceptable );
+
+    __TRY
+    {
+        err = svcctl_NotifyBootConfigStatus( NULL, boot_acceptable );
+    }
+    __EXCEPT(rpc_filter)
+    {
+        err = map_exception_code( GetExceptionCode() );
+    }
+    __ENDTRY
+
+    return set_error( err );
+}
+
+/******************************************************************************
  *     OpenServiceA   (sechost.@)
  */
 SC_HANDLE WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OpenServiceA( SC_HANDLE manager, const char *name, DWORD access )
